  "description": "Conversion of an existing window opening to a new door opening, with the installation of a tri-fold door, the creation of a first floor roof terrace on the existing flat roof,&nbsp; replacement of metal railings with new iron balustrade, installation of new opaque glass balustrade, installation of bicycle enclosure and other associated works. ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed use of the flat roof as a terrace, by reason of its size and location, would have a harmful impact on the living conditions of the adjoining residents, through noise and disturbance, and a loss of privacy. The proposal would also result in substandard accommodation through a loss of outlook and ventilation for the occupiers of Flat H.&amp;nbsp; As such, the proposal is contrary to policies D6 (Housing quality and standards) and D14 (Noise) of the London Plan (2021), policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), LP2 (Development and Amenity), LP17 (Housing Design) and LP58 (Pollution) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020), the guidance contained within Hackney&#x27;s Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2009), and the Technical housing standards – nationally described space standard (2015).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed balustrading to the flat roof, by reason of its poor design and incoherent design approach, fails to represent good design that conserves or enhances and reveals the significance of the locally listed building and its setting. As such, the proposal is contrary to policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets), and LP4 (Non-Designated Heritage Assets) of the Hackney Local Plan LP33 (2020) and policies D3 (Optimising site layout through the design-led approach) and HC1 (Heritage conservation and growth) of The London Plan (2021).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
